http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-editpage.php?page=Mini-dictionary


I think you mean 
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Mini-dictionary&bl .


I think it is a useful document, though it reflects the intent of one 
BPFKJ (Nick) who is no longer active. Robin can and has strayed from that 
document in time past. E.g. the concordance tool that Nick talks about 
doesn't actually exist (we make do with web search and command-line IRC 
log search tools).


Also, Nick's suggestion that "all representative usage" be documented must 
be taken with a grain of salt; for instance, an index of all usages of 
"le" would be less than useless.


